This directory is a book-generation owner section and must exist even when it
holds no records. It holds none: every chapter of every book in this corpus is
generated from lesson markdown, so there are no hand-written chapters left to
own. Git cannot track an empty directory, so this file holds it open.

Read "chapter" strictly. This section covers NUMBERED chapters, and for a while
that was not the same as "everything a book prints as a chapter": seventeen
tracks still had a hand-written `appendix-pronunciation.tex`, which is a
`\chapter*` on the page and was in no owner section at all, so this file read
true while it was not the whole truth. Those are generated now too, from
`<track>/pronunciation-reference.md` via `reference-appendices.d`, and
`shard-cli.ts` fails if any registered track's reference is not.

readStrictDirectory() in book-generation-shards.ts filters this filename out of
the listing. Do not rename it, and delete it only when this section has a real
record again.
